                      (./defs/wildbits.d):00811         * WizFi360 Registers, 2K x 2 FIFO
                      (./defs/wildbits.d):00812         * Wifi_Control_Register:
                      (./defs/wildbits.d):00813         * Bit[0] = 0 = 115,200K Mode, 1 = 921,600K Mode
                      (./defs/wildbits.d):00814         * Bit[1] = 0 Default, 1 = Reset FIFO (you need to bring it back to 0) This is directly connected to reset line of the FIFO
                      (./defs/wildbits.d):00815         * Bit[2] = RX FIFO Empty ( 1 = Empty, 0 = Data Available)
                      (./defs/wildbits.d):00816         * Bit[3] = TX FIFO Empty ( 1 = Empty, 0 = Data Available)
     FF20             (./defs/wildbits.d):00817         WizFi.Base          equ       $FF20
     0008             (./defs/wildbits.d):00818         WizFi.TxEmpty       equ       %00001000
     0004             (./defs/wildbits.d):00819         WizFi.RxEmpty       equ       %00000100
     0002             (./defs/wildbits.d):00820         WizFi.Reset         equ       %00000010
     0001             (./defs/wildbits.d):00821         WizFi.Rate          equ       %00000001
                      (./defs/wildbits.d):00822                             org       $0
